  "findings": [
    "Both cells classify all168 training temporal-presence labels correctly, but no initial168 training capture exists: this is a final training measurement, not a demonstrated training-accuracy gain.",
    "The held-exposed permission variant moves farther into absent territory (-0.405558 initially to -0.478626 CE/-0.493177 margin), while the otherwise paired obligation variant crosses to present (-0.020266 to +0.071098/+0.025659). Head updates are input-dependent, not a uniform bias shift.",
    "The existing training set already contains permission/obligation/prohibition wording with positive and negative temporal labels, and one nearly identical permission/before-date/if/unless template. An entirely unseen permission phrase is not the explanation.",
    "The trainable temporal head receives a mean of frozen contextual span-token features. Contextual/lexical feature interactions and coverage are plausible generalization limitations, but saved output logits do not establish feature-space separability or prove that the frozen encoder is incapable.",
    "A range of thresholds remains perfect on training. The failing exposed permission margin lies inside that unconstrained training gap, so training-perfect accuracy neither identifies a unique threshold nor rules out calibration. A threshold chosen to fix that known row would be exposed-target fitting.",
    "The margin arm leaves the same legacy error and unchanged development/evaluation whole-rule counts, with additional earlier-evaluation regressions. There is no evidence to promote it or to claim that more updates on these168 rows will resolve fidelity."
  ],
